WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.890
We're with Shameeka and Lee.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.920
Also joining us

3
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.410
is the biological father of their children,

4
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.630
as well as 100 more.

5
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.440
And we are here to meet him.

6
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.070
I'm very excited to have a conversation with him.

7
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.800
Ari Nagel, welcome to the show.

8
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.869
Hallo, thank you, so good to be here.

9
00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:21.960
(audience clapping)

10
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.760
Okay.

11
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.700
I want to just ask,

12
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.190
what I wonder if anyone else

13
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.580
has the burning question,

14
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.770
which is,

15
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.040
why do you do this?

16
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.680 line:15%
But you know, I'm from a big family.

17
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.660 line:15%
So in some ways I wanted a big family,

18
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.790 line:15%
but you know,

19
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.180 line:15%
you do it once and you see the mom is happy.

20
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.590
You see the kid is happy and then you do it again.

21
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.680
And then it just ended up growing.

22
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.810
And I was having around two or three kids a year.

23
00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.840
And then I don't know, this year I'm on track to have 30.

24
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.200
I had 25 kids this year so far.

25
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.877
It's been very busy during the pandemic.

26
00:00:55.877 --> 00:00:57.410
(laughs)

27
00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.083
Some people were like getting into baking

28
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:01.730
and you know, and I was just expanding.

29
00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.330
Of course I was traveling a lot.

30
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.450
Do you think that there is any

31
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.710
like God complex in there?

32
00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.830
No, that's a legitimate question you know,

33
00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.480
'cause I have a hundred children.

34
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.530
And people will like, well, why do you need more kids?

35
00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.363
You know?

36
00:01:17.363 --> 00:01:19.640
But if you look at Lee and Shameeka,

37
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.790
they each have one child.

38
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.200
So if I would've told them, sorry, Lee,

39
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.770
I can't help you because I already have

40
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.603
a lot of children

41
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:26.010
and I don't need any more children

42
00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.607
then they would probably say,

43
00:01:27.607 --> 00:01:30.330
yeah, but what about us? We want our one child.

44
00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.520
So I don't focus on how many children I have.

45
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.640
You would focus on the families

46
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.670
that I'm helping grow.

47
00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.920
Now, when you have your children,

48
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.050
do you say, I'll be as involved as you want?

49
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.020
What are the sort of prerequisites?

50
00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.230
Is there a contract?

51
00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.230
Like how do you go into this?

52
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.540
It's always up to the moms.

53
00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.520
So there's some kids that I see all the time.

54
00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.690
And then there's many kids that I've never met.

55
00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:57.970
I was in Israel this past week

56
00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.750
and I got together with two of my children there,

57
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.510
but then the other mom didn't really want me

58
00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.343
to come visit.

59
00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:03.440
So, that's okay, you know,

60
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.640
and I try and play a role wherever I'm wanted or needed.

61
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.630
And I think there's hundred different families.

62
00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:11.240
So each of them have a different idea

63
00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.770
of what role and it's dynamic.

64
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:13.730
It changes all the time.

65
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.780
So sometimes maybe they don't want me to play a role,

66
00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.860
but then maybe the kid's 10 or 11 years old

67
00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.930
and starts asking questions

68
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.920
and then it transitions into something else.

69
00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.553
Okay. Now I just have to ask process.

70
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.666
what is the process?
(laughs)

71
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:28.874
Yeah.

72
00:02:28.874 --> 00:02:31.200
like have there been

73
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.280
actual,

74
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.113
intimate,

75
00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:34.910
physical encounters,

76
00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.480
the old fashioned way?

77
00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.670
It varied.

78
00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.330
So, you know I have a hundred kids.

79
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.530
So there's lots of different ways to make a baby.

80
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.800
The vast majority of them,

81
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.554
I just put it into a cup

82
00:02:46.554 --> 00:02:47.430
and, you know, and I gave it to them

83
00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.430
and they put it inside.

84
00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.640
It is the soft cup handoff.

85
00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.140
Exactly. And that works.

86
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.620
It works the same as if we did it the old fashioned way.

87
00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.320
I mean, you've met people at, you know,

88
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.070
different places whenever these windows arrive.

89
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.310
That's right, yeah.

90
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.810
Okay, how the heck are you juggling all of this?

91
00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.483
Like I have two kids.
(laughs)

92
00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:09.316
Yeah

93
00:03:09.316 --> 00:03:10.990
I am spread so thin.

94
00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.160
Like how are you like,

95
00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.910
legitimately being like,

96
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.930
I'll be there to help you with your kids.

97
00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.460
I'll meet you there.

98
00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.050
Who is running your schedule?

99
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.480
How are you doing that?

100
00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.457
Yep.

101
00:03:22.457 --> 00:03:23.290
(audience clapping)

102
00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.850
I don't have any unpaid interns.

103
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.150
You know, I'm working on my schedule.

104
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.020
So it's challenging,

105
00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.130
and it's especially challenging because it's hard to plan.

106
00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.780
I don't know when they're gonna be fertile.

107
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.250
So you really don't know sometimes

108
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.310
until the last minute.

109
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.390
So like I have a woman ovulating tomorrow in Atlanta

110
00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.460
and then on Saturday in Jacksonville,

111
00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.710
but I also have a baby being born on Tuesday.

112
00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.020
So I'm gonna need to get back for that birth,

113
00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.150
because I want to be there.

114
00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.050
She's a single mom,

115
00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.510
so I want to make sure I'm there

116
00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.910
for the delivery room.

117
00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.880
So I didn't buy my flight yet, but yeah,

118
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.250
sometimes it's challenging.

119
00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.610
And then sometimes you have two women

120
00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.710
ovulating on the same day

121
00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.390
and then you have to decide, well,

122
00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:56.600
who am I gonna help? You know?

123
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.360
So do you help the older woman

124
00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.450
who maybe is running out of time

125
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.520
or do you help the younger woman

126
00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.610
who maybe can try next month,

127
00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.070
but has probably a much higher chance of conceiving?

128
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.630
Well, and that circles a little bit back

129
00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.790
to a God complex.

130
00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.530
Like who do you choose in that scenario?

131
00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.363
Yeah.

132
00:04:10.363 --> 00:04:11.420
Well ultimately in the end,

133
00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.410
the good news is that they may ovulate every month.

134
00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.380
So you might say, listen, I'm not free this month,

135
00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.340
but let's try again.

136
00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.170
Or sometimes I'll just work up the effort

137
00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.490
and try twice in one day.

138
00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.213
But ideally that's not the best case scenario.

139
00:04:22.213 --> 00:04:23.740
What does the future hold for you?

140
00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.990
Do you have any plans?

141
00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.150
What is Ari doing?

142
00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.765
Yeah, that's a good question, you know.

143
00:04:29.765 --> 00:04:30.760
There are increased risks

144
00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.190
I think for the age of the male,

145
00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.650
even though physically I'm capable of continuing

146
00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.773
to have children until my old age.

147
00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:39.960
I think that some people link autism perhaps

148
00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:40.900
to the age of the males.

149
00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.780
So no, I think my retirement's gonna happen.

150
00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.040
You know, it's hard, because you know,

151
00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.320
I'm going to Jacksonville on Saturday

152
00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.600
for this woman who is ovulating, right.

153
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.140
And we have a three-year-old daughter

154
00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.460
and she wants a sibling for her daughter.

155
00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.650
So what am I supposed to tell her you know?

156
00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.483
It would be hard.

157
00:04:55.483 --> 00:04:57.150
So it would have to be some kind of phased retirement

158
00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.950
where if it's the family that I already helped

159
00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.005
and they want the same father for both their children,

160
00:05:01.005 --> 00:05:03.190
then that's something it'll be a little hard to say no,

161
00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.253
but maybe it's a new couple, maybe somehow.

162
00:05:05.253 --> 00:05:07.960
But you're mindful that eventually medically

163
00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.200
things do change for a male

164
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.390
and you're cognizant of every aspect.

165
00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.400
Yes, and I think it's different

166
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.620
if you're starting a family of your own,

167
00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.690
but if you're helping other women grow their families,

168
00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:17.930
then they could find someone younger.

169
00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:18.990
Of course my son is 18,

170
00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.700
but he is not interested in taking over

171
00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:21.533
the family business.

172
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:23.557
(laughs)

173
00:05:24.839 --> 00:05:25.672
Yeah.

174
00:05:25.672 --> 00:05:28.722
(audience clapping)

175
00:05:28.722 --> 00:05:31.990
Well Ari, Shameeka and Lee, you guys, thank you.

176
00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.053
Thank you.

177
00:05:34.053 --> 00:05:34.886
(audience clapping)

178
00:05:34.886 --> 00:05:36.442
Really and truly,

179
00:05:36.442 --> 00:05:37.573
and thanks for hanging out

180
00:05:37.573 --> 00:05:40.390
and listening and to every-one at home.

181
00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:41.843
This was really just,

182
00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.900
it's hard to put into words,

183
00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.080
but I'm very grateful to have this conversation.

184
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.663
(upbeat music)

